        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Todd Phillips, Scot Armstrong, Breckin Meyer, Seann William Scott, Paulo Costanzo, DJ Qualls\n- Products: Road Trip, Old School, Starsky & Hutch, The Hangover Trilogy, Due Date, War Dogs\n- Topics: filmography, comedy films, plot premise\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Todd Phillips co-wrote and directed the American comedy film Road Trip.\n- In 2000, Scot Armstrong and Todd Phillips wrote the film Road Trip.\n- In 2000, Road Trip starred Breckin Meyer, Seann William Scott, Paulo Costanzo, and DJ Qualls.\n- In Road Trip, four college friends embark on an 1800-mile journey to retrieve an illicit tape that was mistakenly mailed to a girlfriend.\n- Todd Phillips is best known for writing and directing Road Trip, Old School, Starsky & Hutch, The Hangover Trilogy, Due Date, and War Dogs.\n- Todd Phillips wrote and directed Old School in 2003, Starsky & Hutch in 2004, The Hangover Trilogy in 2009, 2011, and 2013, Due Date in 2010, and War Dogs in 2016.",
